    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju held a glass, a butter paper and a book in front of a torch.\n\"They behave differently,\" he said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "luminous",
     "transparent",
     "opaque"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Objects that give out light on their own are luminous, like the Sun and a torch. Others, like the Moon, only reflect light.\nTransparent materials such as glass let almost all light pass so we see clearly through them. Translucent materials such as butter paper let some light pass. Opaque materials such as wood and metal block light.\nLight travels in straight lines, which is why we cannot see through a bent pipe."
    }
   },
